mode: "100644"
text: "# Mechanics, stacks & worked examples\n\n## The mechanic menu (pick by job + friction)\n| Mechanic | Friction | Best job | Where it lives |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Poll | one tap | decisions, relatable splits, validation | native sticker (human adds) / feed \"comment A or B\" |\n| Emoji slider | one drag | nuanced feeling (\"how excited?\") | native sticker (human adds) |\n| Quiz | a tap + payoff | teach via play, myth-busting | native sticker / feed \"guess in comments\" |\n| Question box (scoped AMA) | typing | depth, connection, content engine | native sticker; answers batched into a series |\n| This-or-that | one comment | genuine debate | feed post (WoopSocial publishes) |\n| Caption-this | creative comment | fun, community energy | feed post |\n| Add-Yours / challenge | create + post | UGC, community threads | native sticker / hashtag challenge (route rights to ugc-and-influencer) |\n| Live AMA / Q&A | attendance | trust, real-time connection | native live (human runs; livestream-and-realtime) |\n\n**Per-platform reality (2026 — verify-quarterly):** the sticker set above (poll / emoji slider / quiz / question\n/ Add-Yours) is Instagram Stories; native poll *posts* also exist on X, LinkedIn, Threads, and YouTube (Community\ntab, which also has quizzes) — Facebook polls live in Groups/Stories; TikTok has Q&A plus poll/quiz stickers on\nvideos. All are created in-app by the human (same native-only rule); a collab/co-authored post is a distribution\nmechanic, not a participation ask → `collabs-and-cross-promotion`.\n\n## Classic stacks (escalating friction)\nPoll → Question (\"tried X? yes/no\" → \"what happened?\") · Quiz → Slider (\"answer\" → \"how confident were you?\") ·\nCountdown → Poll (\"launch in 3 days\" → \"will you be there?\") · Poll result → follow-up content (\"78% said X — so\nhere's the fix\").\n\n## Cadence that compounds\nRecurring, named slots beat random asks: a Monday decision poll, a Wednesday quiz, a Friday scoped AMA. Consistency\ntrains participation; variety keeps it fresh. Track which mechanics *your* audience actually uses and double down.\n\n## Worked example A — \"Blunt indie founder\" (decision poll, loop closed)\nStory 1 (human adds poll sticker): \"two landing page headlines. which one? A: 'invoices that get paid.' B: 'stop\nchasing payments.'\" → Story 2 next day: \"1,204 votes, 71% said B. shipping it this week — you named the product's\nvoice. next decision coming friday.\" — real decision, one tap, result shared, ownership created.\n\n## Worked example B — \"Warm bookkeeping studio\" (scoped AMA → series)\nStory 1 (human adds question box): \"It's tax-prep week — ask me anything about *getting ready for your first\nfiling as a freelancer*. I'll answer the best ones here all week (first names off unless you say otherwise).\" →\nStories 2-6: one question per day, answered warmly, batched from the box. — scoped ask, permissioned, one box\nfeeding a week of content.\n\n## Never\nRun filler polls with no job · leave a loop unclosed · post a bare \"AMA\" · rig or fabricate results · astroturf\nquestions from fake accounts · punish wrong quiz answers · fabricate quiz facts · harvest sensitive data via\ncasual polls (answers aren't anonymous) · expose an individual's answer without consent · claim WoopSocial\nattaches stickers or auto-DMs · dress a Story poll up as research.\n"
